voice lines  what's more the enemies in this game  aren't very varied either it's there's  like a handful of different enemies and  some just take more bullets and others  that's that's like the main thing  in it's just all very met in that  department gameplay-wise  this is where the game really shines as  an action-platformer your game has to  have tight controls and for the most  part this is very true of this title  there are a few times of any that I felt  like I jumped and didn't go where I was  supposed to go the game also utilizes a  gun for rad and I wish I cared more  about this element the gun itself fires  just fine the game offers like different  temporary upgrades for the gun although  I like the idea of them implementing an  RPG element where you can upgrade your  done and things like that that would  make it feel a bit more important like  it's like the gun mattered you know you  can fire with the Y button are the zr  button and this is important because  this helps you aim your gun with the  right stick you still have to take your  thumb off to jump but this adds accuracy  and you know seeing us how this was a PC  game I can see why they want to have  something like that this title that  being said the fact you still take your  thumb off the stick to jump feels of  like a missed opportunity to add another  button for your jump button that way you  could keep your thumb on the stick you  know I mean it's it's just it's weird  it's weird and I feel like they would  have added to the game that being said  the game is full of collectibles from  gems to hats characters and artwork this  game has a lot for you it really wants  you to replay levels Explorer so this  game does have some semblance of replay  value and to be honest it had better  because some of the levels can really  stretch especially if you don't know  where you're going what I mean is the  first level in the game took me 5  minutes tops to complete every level  afterward we'll tired at least 15  minutes and this is because in order to  complete a level you have to collect 4  parts of a key that opens the exit gate  in the first level it was pretty  straightforward I mean you go from left  to right and you basically run into the  key parts as you go but in other levels  it becomes much more of a maze and my  goodness  it can get very frustrating I'm not  proud of this but one level had me  locked into a 30 minute struggle why  because I didn't know that the game had  sub keys these smaller keys open up  doors that lead to the rest of the level  I mistook one of these doors to be an  exit gate and so I searched half of the  level for two key fragments that weren't  there  now don't get me wrong I would take this  upon myself if I could actually see the  keyhole in this ridiculously low  resolution title and this is where  things like graphics can matter but I  digress the game itself is very fun like  I said they're their little puzzles here  and there that I really enjoyed there  are parts of this level that contained  the pixel verse it's like a place with  that dusty which is rad sentient game  console goes to repair missing parts of  the main level these segments are right  like there's nothing too remarkable to  say about them they're mainly like two  forms of one is which like you go  through a maze and search for missing  parts and then the other you have to  connect an electrical puzzle and that  one that kind is much more rewarding I  like that one  much better in between levels are little  mini games you can do like some are  memory games others or like a pogo stick  thing there's like even like a pinball  game so there's that if you're into  mini-games lastly I will mention that  you can play this game in coop so if you  have someone you'd like to play this  title with there you go you can do that  there's the battle modes and you can  also work together  this game is not for children do not let  the boxart fool you this game is very  very 